> more [time] [...]

No freezes for >22h, seems to be fine.


> [...] and will afterwards disable IOMMU as a whole to see if I hit
> USB and PCI(e) issues again with that combination.

The systems seems to run stable with CONFIG_IOMMU_SUPPORT=3Dn set, too. T=
his is
expected.
However: unlike during earlier tests when I disabled IOMMU and Intel IOMM=
U via
kernel/boot parameters, I am not seeing any DMA mapping errors.

There seems to be a difference between disabling IOMMU/Intel IOMMU static=
ally in
the kernel compared to disabling it via kernel parameter. Is this another=
 bug?

I've attached both kernel ring buffer logs (minus the timings for easier =
diffing.)

  [*] kern-new-iommu_off.log.bz2 disables IOMMU and Intel IOMMU via boot =
parameter
  [*] kern-iommu_static_off.log.bz2 has CONFIG_IOMMU_SUPPORT=3Dn set and =
any IOMMU
support statically disabled (also consequently DMAR)



